# ---- S0920v Vigil of St Matthew pp. 564-565 (pdf 321)
LA0=F.A.RD['S0920v'][0]['la']
NEWLA="Benedíctio Dómini super caput justi. Ideo dedit illi Dóminus hereditátem, et divísit illi partem in tríbubus duódecim: et invénit grátiam in conspéctu omnis carnis. Et magnificávit eum in timóre inimicórum, et in verbis suis monstra placávit. Glorificávit illum in conspéctu regum, et jussit illi coram pópulo suo, et osténdit illi glóriam suam. In fide et lenitáte ipsíus sanctum fecit illum, et elégit eum ex omni carne. Et dedit illi coram præcépta, et legem vitæ et disciplínæ: et excélsum fecit illum. Státuit ei testaméntum ætérnum, et circumcínxit eum zona justítiæ, et índuit eum Dóminus corónam glóriæ."
RAW('data/readings33.js',['S0920v',0,'la'],LA0,NEWLA,'M39 pp. 564-565 (pdf 321)','the Missal prints a shortened text ("duódecim : et invénit grátiam in conspéctu omnis carnis. Et magnificávit"; no "Diléctus Deo ... Móyses"); "disciplínæ : et excélsum"; and the ending after the page break "et índuit eum Dóminus corónam glóriæ." was missing (the site stopped at "índuit eum"). Same text as G369/S1129v (A3, p. 320), with this page\'s commas')
RAW('data/readings33.js',['S0920v',0,'en'],F.A.RD['S0920v'][0]['en'],"The blessing of the Lord is upon the head of the just. Therefore did the Lord give him an inheritance, and divided him his portion among the twelve tribes: and he found grace in the sight of all flesh. And he magnified him in the fear of his enemies, and by his words he made prodigies to cease. He glorified him in the sight of kings, and gave him commandments in the sight of his people, and showed him his glory. He sanctified him in his faith and meekness, and chose him out of all flesh. And he gave him commandments before his face, and a law of life and instruction: and he exalted him. He made an everlasting covenant with him, and girded him about with a girdle of justice, and the Lord put on him a crown of glory.",'M39 pp. 564-565 (pdf 321)','the English was Douay Eccli 44:26-45:9 (Moses, Aaron\'s priesthood), which the Missal\'s Latin does not have; the Missal departs from the Vulgate, so the English follows the Missal\'s Latin (Joseph 27 Nov 23:00), labelled AI; wording as A3\'s G369/S1129v')
FX.append({"file":"data/readings33.js","op":"add","path":["S0920v",0,"en_src"],"old":None,"new":"ai","src":"M39 pp. 564-565 (pdf 321)","why":"label: AI translation of the Missal's Latin (it departs from the Vulgate; Joseph 27 Nov 23:00)"})
P('S0920v','r1',[1,2,3,4],'M39 p. 565 (pdf 321)',why='as printed: "in domo sua : Et erat"; "Scribæ"; "publicánis et peccatóribus manducátis et bíbitis?"')
